Changes made to just-bash, as required by section 4(b) of the license:

- The code is split into a core package and optional add-on packages
  (python, js, sqlite, net, html, archive). Core loads each add-on by package
  name and reports a missing one instead of failing at import time.
- Modified files in packages/just-bash/src:
  - addons.ts (new): the seam through which the slim build loads add-ons.
  - commands/registry.ts: reports a missing add-on (exit 127) and requires
    the python and javascript add-ons when those options are set.
  - network/fetch.ts: requires the net add-on when the network option is set.
  - commands/python3/python3.ts: starts the worker shipped by the add-on and
    passes it CPython compiled once per process.
  - commands/python3/worker.ts: instantiates CPython from that module.
  - commands/sqlite3/sqlite3.ts: starts the worker shipped by the add-on.
  - commands/tar/archive.ts: names the archive add-on when xz or zstd is
    unavailable.
- Packaging: pure-JavaScript dependencies are bundled into each package,
  the CommonJS, browser, and CLI builds are not published, the typescript
  dependency is removed, guarded-fetch is updated to 0.1.5, and the
  supported Node.js range starts at 22.13.

The full list of differences is in the repository README.
